Occasionally I have found myself in the dark, and with no light to see
by. Mapping gehennon one step at a time, for example. And with surplus
wishes I can use... So I decided to run through the various sources of
light in Nethack;

+ light
	feature:
		lights big area
	cons:
		single shot (i.e. must be cast again and again as you move - only
feasible for a wizard or others with the Eye of Aethiopica), uses
power

? and / light
	feature:
		as the spell
		cheap to write scroll
		wand can be recharged
	cons:
		single shot, scroll disappears and wand loses a charge

oil-lamp and brass lantern
	feature:
		movable
		lights medium area
	cons:
		runs out

Sunsword
	feature:
		movable
		lights small area
		permanent
	cons:
		must be wielded
		pretty useless weapon
		blasts N and C
		wishing for artifacts is risky

Eyes of the Overworld
	feature:
		movable
		lights medium area
		works through walls
		permanent
	cons:
		must be worn (though this is less of a problem)
		can only be used by Neutrals
		wishing for artifacts is risky

Magic lamp
	feature:
		movable
		lights medium area
		can give a wish
		permanent
	cons:
		cannot be wished for

YANI: So what I propose is a permanent lightsource that can be wished
for - like a magic lamp without the wishes. Perhaps call it the
longlife-bulb brass lantern or something.

llb-brass lantern
	feature:
		movable
		lights medium area
		permanent

	cost about 30 credits
	same tile as standard brass lantern; id'ed by price or longevity
	rubbing should give typical brass lantern result.

